From eea1582db102a9d47c7e38c51251a1b3fa5d0d0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: codEx Fork Bot <codex-fork-bot@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:50:30 +0800
Subject: rewind: drop legacy snapshot chain compatibility

- Removes the workspace-wide legacy chain, the copy-based manifest
  compatibility (object ids are now required), and the chain-walking
  restore fallback: every snapshot is content-addressed and
  self-contained, so restore fails loudly when a physical copy is
  missing instead of searching older snapshots.
- Simplifies the engine API to thread-scoped functions only:
  take_snapshot/list_snapshots/restore_snapshot all take a thread id,
  and the workspace listing aggregates conversation chains only.
- Manifest format is bumped to version 2; no historical snapshot layouts
  are read anymore.
